# API license / ToS compliance

When connecting or extending any third-party API or data feed (Twitch Helix, IGDB, twitchdrops.app, Statuspage, PostHog, Telegram, …), implement **in line with that provider’s license, Developer Agreement, ToS, robots.txt, and documented integration rules**.

## Before first use (and when changing usage)

1. **Find the rules** — official ToS / Developer Agreement / Trademark / rate-limit docs / `robots.txt`. If none are published, treat the public documented API as the ceiling; do not scrape HTML/pages that are not part of the documented API.
2. **Paid fees / tariffs** — before enabling a platform capability (BotFather toggles, API products, add-ons, higher limits, forum/topics modes, ads, payouts, …), read the provider ToS **and** pricing / payments docs for **extra commissions, withheld %, subscription tiers, or one-time fees**. Surface cost and scope to the user **before** implementing or shipping (who pays, % or amount, bot-wide vs per-user, how to turn off). Do not assume a free UI toggle is free for the developer.
3. **Prefer official / documented endpoints** over scraping, unofficial GQL, or reverse-engineered clients.
4. **Attribution** — if the provider requires (or clearly expects) source credit, show it in user-facing copy and/or README. Keep a clear path from displayed data back to the source (links).
5. **Rate limits & caching** — honor documented limits and `Cache-Control` / `Retry-After` / `429` where applicable; poll no faster than needed.
6. **Commercial / redistribution** — do not sell raw API metadata dumps; Premium may charge for *our* product features that *use* API data, not for reselling the data itself. When unsure, ask before shipping.
7. **Auth & privacy** — OAuth scopes least-privilege; do not log tokens; privacy notices for user data collected via the API.
8. **Marks** — Twitch (and other) trademarks only per trademark guidelines; do not imply affiliation/endorsement when the provider forbids it.

## Checklist (PR)

- [ ] Endpoint is documented / allowed (not a disallowed scrape path)
- [ ] Provider ToS / pricing checked for fees tied to the new capability; costs disclosed to the user if non-zero
- [ ] Attribution / disclaimer updated if required
- [ ] Polling/caching respects provider guidance
- [ ] No new secret hardcoding; scopes minimal
- [ ] Self-check or comment notes any intentional gray-area (e.g. unofficial endpoint) with upgrade path

## Known fee traps (do not rediscover)

| Provider | Capability | Fee | Authority |
|---|---|---|---|
| Telegram | Topics in private chats (BotFather Threaded Mode) | **15%** withheld from **all** Stars purchases on that bot while enabled (not per end-user `topics_enabled`) | [Bot Developer ToS §6.2.6](https://telegram.org/tos/bot-developers) |
## Twitch Helix (baseline)

Authority: [Twitch Developer Services Agreement](https://legal.twitch.com/legal/developer-agreement) + [API guide](https://dev.twitch.tv/docs/api/guide).

- Use Helix with registered Client-ID / secrets from env
- Respect rate limits — `TwitchClient` session retries HTTP 429 using `Retry-After` / `Ratelimit-Reset`
- Attribute / link back to Twitch content when displaying Program Materials; show `twitch_not_affiliated` + OAuth privacy (`/privacy`, `with_oauth_legal`)
- Do not sell or redistribute Helix metadata as a dataset
- Do **not** use unofficial `gql.twitch.tv` — Chat Mini App has no About/panels Info UI (Helix has no panels API)
- **Exception (AI clips only):** `ai_clips.py` may call `gql.twitch.tv` solely for VOD chat replay (`VideoCommentsByOffsetOrCursor`, time-offset scan) to pick clip moments. No other GQL. Code comments + self-check must name this gray area; upgrade path = official VOD chat API if Twitch ships one.

## IGDB

Prefer partner [CSV data dumps](https://api-docs.igdb.com/#data-dumps) over live Apicalypse for new game-metadata features — see [`igdb-dumps.mdc`](igdb-dumps.mdc) (includes **Commercial Usage Addendum** constraints: Permitted Purpose, no selling dumps, partner ClientID, attribution wording, termination survival).

- Attribution copy (EN): `Games metadata is powered by IGDB.com` → link [IGDB.com](https://www.igdb.com); helper `i18n.igdb_attribution`
- Do not redistribute IGDB metadata as a paid dataset; Premium = product features, not data resale
- ClientID / partner contact email changes → written notice to Twitch (not only local `.env`)
